  "interpretation": [
    "DurableFlush is the actual journal.Flush(true) timer. About half the observed write wall is cumulative durable flushing; the interval includes tiny freeze/normal-Stop and concurrent maintenance overhead. It is not an OS latency breakdown.",
    "User flush labels charge the final operation of a shared barrier. 299970/215200 is an aggregate commits-per-charged-flush proxy, not native callback batch size. Metadata/resize/write flush time is not exclusively caused by the labeled operation.",
    "The slowest saved interval has no additional recorded relocations or packing completions, yet flush latency rises sharply. It identifies a barrier-latency stall; it does not prove the disk, OS, another process or background index work caused the latency.",
    "Commit times Apply per mutation; FlushPendingWrites calls FlushIndexBatch before its own barrier timer. Shared deferred node/path/name/page persistence therefore falls outside per-operation ApplyTicks and that final barrier timing. It remains inside actual wall time. Do not assign all wall-minus-flush time to index work.",
    "WinFsp CompleteMetadata holds its mutation gate while ApplyMutationBatch/CommitStorageBatch flushes. Close/GetFileInfo waits in the saved stack are downstream contention, not extra additive elapsed time. Journal waitingMutations excludes the upstream native FIFO, so maxWaitingMutations=1 does not disprove eight application workers or identify queue occupancy.",
    "Packing chunks 63 relocation records plus a packing-state progress record per group of 64. Most shared barriers are charged to packing-state; the relocation-only flush count understates packing barrier count. Packing is journal/index amplification more than directly measured flush time.",
    "BuildPackingPlan selects when descriptor.Length-liveUnion>=4096 with liveUnion>0; it has no live/dead fraction or relocation-row cost screen. First journal-to-raw packing may be useful; repeating packed-object packing for small dead payload can move most live rows again. Actual reclaimed bytes and per-job copy/index cost were not recorded, so wasted work in this fixture is not quantified."
  ],
